=== HOOK_PORT ===

useGuard.ts:
  + Added @deprecated JSDoc to all 5 exports (useGuardConfig, useGuardEvents,
    useSetGuardConfig, useGuardPanic, useAcknowledgeGuardEvent).
  + Documents that /vehicles/{id}/guard* routes were deleted with
    guard_handler.go and guard_events table by Phase-42/0077.
  + Hooks retained because in-scope GuardModePage AND out-of-scope
    GuardModeWidget still import them; surface 404 gracefully via
    PageContainer.error per ADR-005 #1.
  + Locked-policy continuation from Phase-43/0023 useVampireDrainStats,
    /0024 useSignalCatalog, /0025 4-deprecated-hooks, /0026 useTrip,
    /0027 useLocations+useGeofences.

useVehicleSystems.ts:
  No changes — keeping legacy `@/types/vehicle-systems` types.
  Rationale: backend climate_handler emits snake_case (inside_temp,
  outside_temp, driver_temp_setting); resilience.ts:19-34 camelCaseKeys
  RETAINS both keys at runtime so the camelCase ClimateState in
  @/types/vehicle-systems matches the wire shape exactly. Switching to
  api/types.ts ClimateSnapshot (which uses inside_temp_c suffix not
  emitted by the backend) would BREAK every page field access.
  Reconciliation deferred to a coordinated prompt that can touch both
  backend mappings AND frontend types.

useWatch.ts:
  No changes — types already match backend WatchSummary wire shape;
  range_km is computed server-side via RatedRange * 1.60934 (see
  internal/api/watch_handler.go); inside_temp_c / outside_temp_c are
  already emitted in °C SI.

=== PAGE_PORT ===

TirePressurePage.tsx (PRE-EXISTING BUG FIX):
  Before: legacy `useSettings.convertPressure(bar)` was called on raw
          backend values, but Phase-42 normalize.toSI converts
          TpmsPressure{Fl,Fr,Rl,Rr} to Pascals (units_test.go: 2.2 bar
          input → 220000 Pa output). Treating Pa input as Bar inflated
          all displayed values by ~10000x.
  After:  - Added useUnits hook + convertPressureFromSI import.
          - Replaced thresholds with Pa scalars:
              NORMAL_MIN_PA = 250_000  (was NORMAL_MIN_BAR = 2.5)
              NORMAL_MAX_PA = 350_000  (was NORMAL_MAX_BAR = 3.5)
              SOFT_LOW_PA   = 200_000  (was 2.0 inline)
              SOFT_HIGH_PA  = 400_000  (was 4.0 inline)
              GAUGE_MAX_PA  = 500_000  (was GAUGE_MAX_BAR = 5.0)
          - pressureColor(pa) and pressureStatus(pa) signatures updated.
          - Added toDisplayPressure(pa) helper:
              convertPressureFromSI(pa / 1000, unitPrefs.pressure)
            Pa → kPa boundary conversion (lib expects kPa per
            unitConversion.ts:185). Same boundary-fix pattern as
            Phase-43/0022 useDriveDetailData (`tp.tirePressureFl/1000`).
          - All 5 callsites updated:
              gaugeMax (line ~172)
              chartData fl/fr/rl/rr (lines ~228-231)
              historyColumns table render (line ~252)
              RadialGauge value (line ~358)
              MetricCard avg/min (lines ~378+388)

ClimateControlPage.tsx (CONSOLIDATION):
  Before: legacy `useSettings.convertTemp/tempUnit` consumed °C input
          and produced display unit. Mathematically correct because
          backend already emits insideTemp/outsideTemp/driverTempSetting
          in °C SI, but inconsistent with phase-43 useUnits convention.
  After:  - Added useUnits + convertTempFromSI import.
          - Removed useSettings import.
          - convertTemp wrapped via local arrow:
              (celsius) => convertTempFromSI(celsius, tempUnit)
            Mathematically identical to legacy convertTemp (both pass
            through ±32 °F formula).
          - convertedChartData useMemo dep list switched from
            [chronoHistory, convertTemp] to [chronoHistory, tempUnit]
            so the closure-captured fn doesn't trigger re-renders on
            unrelated settings churn (precedent: Phase-43/0022).
          - All 9 convertTemp callsites preserved (lines 275, 307, 314,
            322, 371-373, 489, 502, 515, 522, 808) — no behavioural
            change because the derived tempUnit is identical to the
            legacy useSettings tempUnit.

SafetySettingsPage.tsx (PRE-EXISTING BUG FIX):
  Before: rendered `latest.miles_since_reset` and
          `latest.self_driving_miles_since_reset` as raw numbers with
          subtitle="miles", but Phase-42 routing.yaml documents both
          MilesSinceReset and SelfDrivingMilesSinceReset as
          UnitKindDistance → normalized to METERS by units.ToSI in the
          unit_history boundary. Rendering 100km of meters as "100000
          miles" was a 1609x display inflation.
  After:  - Added useUnits + convertDistanceFromSI imports.
          - Computed distanceUnit = unitPrefs.distance.
          - MetricCard values wrapped in:
              fmtNumber(convertDistanceFromSI(meters, distanceUnit))
            with subtitle now showing the actual unit (`distanceUnit` or
            i18n distanceAutopilot interpolation).
          - i18n keys added: safety.distanceSinceReset,
            safety.selfDrivingDistance, safety.distanceAutopilot
            (preserved milesSinceReset/miles/selfDrivingMiles/
            milesAutopilot per never-delete rule from Phase-43/0002).

GuardModePage.tsx (NO-OP):
  No changes — page already uses no SI conversion (only renders
  lat/lng/timestamps/event_type strings). The 5 useGuard.ts hooks it
  imports are now @deprecated; backend 404s on /guard requests will
  surface via PageContainer.error per ADR-005 #1.

MaintenancePage.tsx (DEFER):
  internal/api/maintenance_handler.go reads Redis "Odometer" signal as
  `currentOdometer`, then mixes with hardcoded literal interval_miles
  values (10000, 20000, 50000) and computes due_mileage as a sum of
  meters + miles. The handler is broken end-to-end and fixing requires:
    1. Backend: switch interval constants to meters and rename JSON
       fields from `current_odometer`/`interval_miles` to SI-suffixed
       equivalents, update due_at/last_serviced calculations.
    2. Frontend: convertDistanceFromSI on display.
  Backend changes are outside the allowed-files set for this prompt.
  Deferral precedent: Phase-43/0026 BE/FE Trip wire-shape mismatch,
  /0027 GeofencesPage field drift, /0029 DataRepairPage adapter set.

MediaPlayerPage.tsx (NO-OP):
  Page only renders playback metadata: now_playing_title/artist/album,
  audio_volume (counts, no unit), now_playing_elapsed/duration (seconds
  for fmtPlayTime). No SI conversion appropriate.

SoftwareUpdatesPage.tsx (NO-OP):
  Page renders version strings, install dates, and counts. No SI
  conversion appropriate.

