=== NOTES ===

1. TirePressurePage Pa→kPa boundary conversion is the third instance of
   the same pre-existing-bug pattern in Phase-43:
     - Phase-43/0022 useDriveDetailData (telemetry distance/speed/temp)
     - Phase-43/0023 BatteryDegradationPage (range_km columns)
     - Phase-43/0030 TirePressurePage (Pa thresholds)
   All three were broken because legacy `useSettings.convertX` helpers
   expected pre-Phase-42 wire-format units (miles, mph, °C, bar) but the
   backend now emits SI baseline units (m, m/s, °C, Pa) after the
   normalize.toSI pipeline.

2. SafetySettingsPage `miles_since_reset` field rendering was broken
   end-to-end: the BACKEND emits SI meters (per routing.yaml MilesSinceReset
   → UnitKindDistance), but the frontend rendered the raw value with a
   "miles" suffix. So a Tesla showing 100km on its odometer would have
   displayed "100000 miles" — a 1609x inflation. Fixed via
   convertDistanceFromSI + dynamic distanceUnit suffix.

3. ClimateControlPage migration is a NO-OP semantic change — `convertTemp`
   wrapped via `(c) => convertTempFromSI(c, tempUnit)` produces identical
   output to the legacy `useSettings.convertTemp` because both apply the
   °F formula `c * 9/5 + 32` to a °C input. The change is for consistency
   with the Phase-43 useUnits convention; pages should not import
   useSettings for unit conversion in the new architecture.

4. useGuard.ts @deprecated continuation of locked-policy precedent
   (Phase-43/0023 useVampireDrainStats, /0024 useSignalCatalog, /0025 4
   hooks, /0026 useTrip, /0027 useLocations+useGeofences). The hooks
   cannot be deleted because in-scope `GuardModePage` and out-of-scope
   `GuardModeWidget` (dashboard) still import them. The old endpoints
   404 gracefully via TanStack Query's error path → PageContainer.error.
   Future replacement: derive guard semantics from existing alert/
   notification rules (separate prompt scope).

5. MaintenancePage deferral rationale: `maintenance_handler.go` is
   structurally broken end-to-end (mixes Redis-backed meters with
   hardcoded literal mile intervals to compute due_mileage). Fixing
   requires both:
     a) Backend handler changes (rename JSON fields, switch intervals
        to meters, update due_at calculation) — OUT of allowed-files.
     b) Frontend convertDistanceFromSI integration — IN allowed-files.
   Per locked-policy, defer until a coordinated prompt can touch both.
   Same pattern as the Phase-43/0026 Trip wire-shape deferral and
   Phase-43/0027 GeofencesPage/dashboard widget field-drift deferral.

6. useVehicleSystems.ts kept on legacy `@/types/vehicle-systems` types
   because:
     a) Backend climate_handler emits snake_case JSON
        (`inside_temp`/`outside_temp`/etc.) without `_c`/`_si` suffixes.
     b) `resilience.ts:19-34` camelCaseKeys RETAINS both snake_case AND
        camelCase keys at runtime, so the legacy camelCase ClimateState
        in @/types/vehicle-systems matches the wire shape EXACTLY.
     c) Switching to api/types.ts ClimateSnapshot (which adds `_c`
        suffix not emitted by the backend) would BREAK every page field
        access in ClimateControlPage at compile time.
   Reconciliation deferred to a future coordinated prompt that can touch
   both backend mappings AND frontend types simultaneously. Same
   reasoning as Phase-43/0026 BE/FE Trip wire-shape deferral.

7. PowerShell-7 quirks captured during gate execution:
   - `$log` Resolve-Path absolute BEFORE Push-Location web (else
     Tee-Object loses the file under web\.github\..., per Phase-46/64,
     /65, /69, Phase-43/0021, /0027, /0029).
   - Use `.\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd` and `npm.cmd run build` instead
     of `npx tsc` and `npm run build` to avoid npm-10's
     "could not determine executable to run" error.
   - Self-deleting gate script must Remove-Item
     `$MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path` BEFORE the git-status check, else
     the untracked `.tmp_gate.ps1` fails the disallowed-file check.

